      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i work a desk job and im pretty out of shape but i want to start lifting weights properly. can u put together a simple 4 week linear progression program for me? mostly just focusing on the big compound lifts like squats, bench, and deadlift so i can get a baseline of strength. thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A simple 4-week linear progression program focusing on the big three—squat, bench, and deadlift—is a great way to start building a baseline. You'll want to keep the volume relatively low to allow for recovery, which is crucial when you're starting out. For the first four weeks, the goal is to add a small amount of weight to your main lifts each session. Remember, consistency is key, so don't skip your warm-ups!\n\nHere is a basic framework:\n\n**Schedule:** Perform this routine 3 times per week, allowing at least one rest day between sessions (e.g., Monday, Wednesday, Friday).\n\n**The Progression:** Start with a weight you can comfortably lift for all sets and reps. Each week, aim to increase the weight by the smallest increment possible (e.g., 2.5 lbs or 5 lbs) on your main lifts.\n\n**The Workouts:**\n\n**Workout A (Focus: Squat & Bench):**\n*   **Squat:** 3 sets of 5 reps\n*   **Bench Press:** 3 sets of 5 reps\n*   **Accessory Work (Choose 1-2):",
